From 47a7ed7432a1a7cd51503dfbafb46cf57e889f70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:53:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 182/185] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: drop the
 CPUCP overlap

The board replaces the SoC's 1 MiB pdp@81300000 region with a 2 MiB
pdp@81200000 one, as the vendor tree of this tablet has a single
CPUCP + PDP region at 0x81200000. The SoC's cpucp@81200000 region was
kept, so both describe 0x81200000..0x812fffff and the kernel logs
"OF: reserved mem: OVERLAP DETECTED!" at every boot.

Delete the SoC's cpucp_mem as well. Nothing references it and the
reserved range stays 0x81200000..0x813fffff, as on stock.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index ba601b94e..de61a1a76 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@
 #include "pmk8850.dtsi"              /* SPMI0: SID-0       */
 #include "qcom-adc5-gen4.h"
 
+/*
+ * The vendor tree has one 2 MiB CPUCP + PDP region at 0x81200000
+ * (pdp_mem below), not the SoC's two 1 MiB regions.
+ */
+/delete-node/ &cpucp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &pdp_mem;
 /delete-node/ &adspslpi_mem;
 
